TRF-27 SplitTryte Rust Programming Primitives Bank v1.0

Locked vocabulary set for Rust programming keywords, primitive types, traits, and common macros.

[LAYOUT]
splitTryte = [11|OPTIONS|BANK_L|VAL_L2|VAL_L1|VAL_L0|BANK_R|VAL_R2|VAL_R1|VAL_R0]
standard_marker = 11

[DESIGN_RULES]

1. Every splitTryte stores two self-contained programming primitives.
2. BANK:+ is Rust core and control flow keywords.
3. BANK:- is Rust primitive types and core monad options.
4. BANK:0 is Rust smart pointers, macros, traits, and async primitives.
5. Full pair table is generated by crossing every left primitive against every right primitive.

[BANK_LANES]

+ = UPPER_ALPHA          = 10
- = LOWER_ALPHA          = 00
0 = NETIV_NUMERIC_SYMBOL = 01

[VAL_LANES]
00 = --- = 00|00|00
01 = --0 = 00|00|01
02 = --+ = 00|00|10
03 = -0- = 00|01|00
